Release History


2024-03 (22-Mar-2024)
=====================

PERFORMANCE:
- Parallelization using OpenMP

ENVIRONMENT:
- Adaptations for compilation with gfortran (often a factor of 2 faster than ifort)


2023-10 (16-Nov-2023)
=====================
FEATURES:
- New default random Se for He and N in Si
- SRIM-2013 electronic stopping powers as an option
- Second tilt angle
- Option to suppress recoils of reentered projectiles in 2D geometries

USER INTERFACE:
- Rename several input parameters to more intuitive names. When the old name
     is used, an error message informs about the new name of the parameter
- Eliminate character arrays from INP file - Use simple arrays instead
- Region 0 need not be specified any more in 2D geometry definitions
- Change (m)imsil.py script to make background execution the default
- Add directory of input (.inp) file to search path of files specified in the 
     INP file
- Adaptive format of x values in HIS file
- Adaptive precision in statistics output to OUT file
- Added times.py script collecting execution times of tests

PERFORMANCE:
- Parallelization using coarrays

ENVIRONMENT:
- Currently, only the Intel compiler is supported
- Build scripts now require Python 3

BUG FIXES:
- Reset ffpmin after ffp without collision. This could have produced artifacts
     near amorphous region boundaries and, in particular when there are many 
     such boundaries like in dynamic simulations
- Avoid ions to be considered subthreshold
- Correct reading of histogram files
- Correct statistical errors of moments in OUT file
- Fix bug in the initialization of Knuth's random number generator


2021-09.2 (25-Oct-2023)
=======================
BUG FIXES:
- Avoid overwriting all masses when specifying ion mass
- Write trajectories of all elements of molecular ions
- Avoid occasional crash when NBOX=0 is specified 
